  "text_input": "Patient presented with a 10-day history of cough with yellowish mucoid expectoration, intermittent fever, and insidious onset breathlessness (MMRC Grade 2) which worsens on exertion. Also reported two episodes of non-projectile, non-bloody vomiting. Known case of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus for 25 years on oral hypoglycemics (Tab Glycomet GP1). History of alcohol use for 20 years. Examination revealed bilateral rhonchi. Investigations showed elevated ESR (51 mm/hr), mild hyperbilirubinemia (1.7 mg/dL), and emphysematous changes on chest X-ray. 2D Echo showed LV diastolic dysfunction with a normal ejection fraction of 55%. USG abdomen revealed Grade 1 fatty liver and Grade 1 prostatomegaly. Diagnosed with acute exacerbation of COPD due to infective etiology and Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. Treated with antibiotics (Inj Tufzone), insulin (Inj Actrapid), and bronchodilators.",
